tion can run. |\n63\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by all Implementations) | The release note and cluster-settings docs must describe what was actually built. |\n64\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by all Implementations) | Docs must reflect validated behavior, including the upgrade-preservation semantics. |\n65\t\n66\tNo konflux-onboarding, repo-onboarding, or license-validation edges: both\n67\tcomponents are established, Konflux-onboarded, and no new dependencies are\n68\tintroduced (only a default value changes).\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n71\t\n72\t| HLR | Priority | Epics | Coverage |\n73\t|---|---|---|---|\n74\t| HLR-1 — default idle culling timeout is 8 hours for new clusters; explicitly configured existing clusters unchanged on upgrade | P1 | E001 (implements the default change and upgrade preservation), E002 (validates culler behavior at the new default and override precedence) | Full |\n75\t| HLR-2 — release note and cluster-settings documentation state the new default and how to override it | P2 | E003 | Full |\n76\t\n77\tNo orphaned requirements. Priority inheritance: E001 and E002 inherit P1 from\n78\tHLR-1. E003 is a `docs-authoring` epic — exempt from priority inheritance;\n79\tderived from strategy frontmatter `priority: Normal` → P2, matching HLR-2.\n80\t\n81\t## Health Warnings\n82\t\n83\t1. **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy omits the Impacted\n84\t   Teams table, per-component change/owner detail, a Dependencies table, formal\n85\t   Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and non-functional requirements. Teams\n86\t   were assigned from architecture-context ownership (Notebooks → Workbenches,\n87\t   Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard); epic acceptance criteria were derived from the\n88\t   HLRs and problem statement.\n89\t2. **Behavior change for existing clusters relying on the old default** (scope\n90\t   note): HLR-1 protects explicitly configured clusters, which implies existing\n