{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b02730e57d5de1d9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9003-E001\n3\ttitle: Change default workbench idle culling timeout to 8 hours\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9003\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 8\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Change default workbench idle culling timeout to 8 hours\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the core change of the strategy: newly installed clusters\n34\tship with a default workbench idle culling timeout of 8 hours instead of 24,\n35\twhile existing clusters that have an explicitly configured value keep their\n36\tconfiguration on upgrade. The idle culling setting, its ConfigMap\n37\t(`notebook-controller-culler-config`), and the Dashboard administration UI\n38\talready exist; this epic changes only the shipped default value and the logic\n39\tthat decides when the default is applied versus when an existing explicit value\n40\tis preserved.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Change the shipped default value of the workbench idle culling timeout from\n45\t  24 hours to 8 hours in the Dashboard's culling configuration handling\n46\t  (OdhDashboardConfig notebookController settings that render the culler\n47\t  configuration).\n48\t- Ensure fresh installs receive the 8-hour default with no admin action\n49\t  required.\n50\t- Ensure upgrade logic does not overwrite an explicitly configured idle culling\n51\t  timeout on clusters that already set one; clusters relying on the previous\n52\t  default (no explicit value) move to the 8-hour default.\n53\t- Update any admin-facing display of the default value in the Dashboard\n54\t  administration UI (placeholders, hints, help text) so it reflects 8 hours.\n55\t- Update/extend unit coverage for the defaulting logic and the\n56\t  upgrade-preservation logic.\n57\t\n58\tOut of scope: per-project/per-user culling policies and any change to activity\n59\tdetection (kernel probe behavior), per the strategy.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- Given a newly installed cluster with no admin configuration, when a workbench\n64\t  is provisioned, then the idle culling timeout default is 8 hours.\n65\t- Given a cluster upgraded from a previous release with an explicitly\n66\t  configured idle culling timeout, when the upgrade completes, then the\n67\t  explicitly configured value is unchanged.\n68\t- Given a cluster upgraded from a previous release with no explicit value\n69\t  (relying on the old 24-hour default), when the upgrade completes, then the\n70\t  effective idle culling timeout is 8 hours.\n71\t- Given an admin needs the previous behavior, when they explicitly configure\n72\t  the idle culling timeout, then the explicit value takes precedence over the\n73\t  default (documented rollback/override path — no feature flag needed since the\n74\t  override mechanism already exists).\n75\t- Unit tests covering the defaulting, upgrade-preservation, and override\n76\t  precedence logic pass in the component's CI/build pipeline.\n77\t\n78\t## HLR Traceability\n79\t\n80\t- HLR-1 (P1): The default idle culling timeout for newly installed clusters is\n81\t  8 hours instead of 24. Existing clusters with an explicitly configured value\n82\t  are not changed on upgrade.\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa8c0ee5f616e604","agent_id":"aabaa0ce7c933167f","session_id":"337c507d-2521-47e2-bad6