{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-936ef843410b0416","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9003-E002\n3\ttitle: Validate workbench culling behavior with the 8-hour default timeout\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9003\n5\tcomponent: Notebooks\n6\tteam: Workbenches\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9003-E001\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 7\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Validate workbench culling behavior with the 8-hour default timeout\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic validates that the workbench idle culler — which requires no code\n35\tchange for this strategy — operates correctly once the shipped default idle\n36\tculling timeout changes to 8 hours. The culler is owned by the Workbenches\n37\tteam, a different team than the one implementing the default change, so this\n38\tvalidation is scoped as its own epic rather than an acceptance criterion on the\n39\timplementing epic. The deliverable is validation evidence that the new default\n40\tbehaves as intended end-to-end and that existing override behavior is\n41\tunaffected.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Validate that workbenches idle beyond the new 8-hour default are stopped by\n46\t  the culler on a cluster running the new default.\n47\t- Validate that workbenches with kernel activity inside the window are not\n48\t  culled (activity detection via Jupyter server API kernel probes continues to\n49\t  work unchanged).\n50\t- Validate that explicitly configured idle culling timeouts (admin-set or\n51\t  per-workbench overrides) take precedence over the new default after upgrade.\n52\t- Validate that no regression is introduced in culling behavior for\n53\t  StatefulSet-backed workbenches (workbenches stop and restart cleanly when\n54\t  culled).\n55\t- Produce a validation report summarizing scenarios, environment, and results.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Given a cluster with the new default and a workbench idle for the configured\n60\t  threshold, when the culling check runs, then the workbench is stopped.\n61\t- Given a cluster with the new default and a workbench with recent kernel\n62\t  activity, when the culling check runs, then the workbench is not culled.\n63\t- Given a cluster with an explicitly configured idle culling timeout, when\n64\t  culling evaluates that workbench, then the explicit value is honored rather\n65\t  than the 8-hour default.\n66\t- A validation report exists documenting the scenarios executed and their\n67\t  results, including any issues found and their disposition.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-1 (P1): The default idle culling timeout for newly installed clusters is\n72\t  8 hours instead of 24. Existing clusters with an explicitly configured value\n73\t  are not changed on upgrade. (This epic provides the Workbenches-team\n74\t  validation of culler behavior under the new default.)\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa8c0ee5f616e604","agent_id":"aabaa0ce7c933167f","session_id":"337c507d-2521-47e2-bad6-58e5af217166","uuid":"b44d6073-68e3-4890-8c1d-1546dde014f6","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:53:33.093Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-936ef843410b0416","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9003 decomposition"}
